{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial\n\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef A(n, k):\n    return factorial(n) // factorial(n - k)\n\ndef solve():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    z = [1]\n    total = 0\n    \n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        # Compute new_z array size\n        new_size = (i - 1) * i // 2 + 1\n        new_z = [0] * new_size\n        \n        # Compute suffix sums d (from right to left)\n        d = [0] * (len(z) + 1)\n        for idx in reversed(range(len(z))):\n            d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + z[idx]) % mod\n        \n        # Fill new_z using d with bounds\n        for w in range(new_size):\n            left_bound = max(0, w + 1 - i)\n            right_bound = min(len(z) - 1, w)\n            new_z[w] = (d[left_bound] - d[right_bound + 1]) % mod\n        \n        # Compute prefix sums e and f\n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for idx in range(len(e) - 1):\n            e[idx + 1] = (e[idx] + d[idx]) % mod\n            f[idx + 1] = (f[idx] - idx * d[idx]) % mod\n        \n        # Calculate bbb contribution\n        bbb = 0\n        R = len(z)\n        \n        # First segment\n        start1 = max(0, len(z) - i)\n        end1 = len(z) - 2\n        for jj in range(start1, end1):\n            L = jj + 2\n            val = (e[R] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R] - f[L])\n            bbb = (bbb + val * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        # Second segment\n        for jj in range(len(z) - i):\n            L = jj + 2\n            R2 = i + jj\n            val = (e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) + (f[R2 + 1] - f[L])\n            bbb = (bbb + val * z[jj]) % mod\n        \n        # Update total\n        total = (total + bbb * A(n, n - i)) % mod\n        z = new_z\n    \n    print(total % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long factorial(int n) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        result *= i;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nlong long A(int n, int k) {\n    return factorial(n) / factorial(n - k);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    \n    if (n == 1) {\n        cout << 0 << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    vector<long long> z = {1};\n    long long total = 0;\n    \n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {\n        // Compute new_z array size\n        int new_size = (i - 1) * i / 2 + 1;\n        vector<long long> new_z(new_size, 0);\n        \n        // Compute suffix sums d (from right to left)\n        vector<long long> d(z.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (int idx = (int)z.size() - 1; idx >= 0; idx--) {\n            d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + z[idx]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Fill new_z using d with bounds\n        for (int w = 0; w < new_size; w++) {\n            int left_bound = max(0, w + 1 - i);\n            int right_bound = min((int)z.size() - 1, w);\n            new_z[w] = (d[left_bound] - d[right_bound + 1]) % mod;\n            if (new_z[w] < 0) new_z[w] += mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Compute prefix sums e and f\n        vector<long long> e(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        vector<long long> f(d.size() + 1, 0);\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < (int)d.size(); idx++) {\n            e[idx + 1] = (e[idx] + d[idx]) % mod;\n            f[idx + 1] = (f[idx] - (long long)idx * d[idx]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Calculate bbb contribution\n        long long bbb = 0;\n        int R = z.size();\n        \n        // First segment\n        int start1 = max(0, (int)z.size() - i);\n        int end1 = (int)z.size() - 2;\n        for (int jj = start1; jj <= end1; jj++) {\n            int L = jj + 2;\n            long long val = ((e[R] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) % mod + (f[R] - f[L])) % mod;\n            bbb = (bbb + val * z[jj]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Second segment\n        for (int jj = 0; jj < (int)z.size() - i; jj++) {\n            int L = jj + 2;\n            int R2 = i + jj;\n            long long val = ((e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + jj) % mod + (f[R2 + 1] - f[L])) % mod;\n            bbb = (bbb + val * z[jj]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Update total\n        total = (total + bbb * A(n, n - i)) % mod;\n        z = new_z;\n    }\n    \n    total %= mod;\n    if (total < 0) total += mod;\n    cout << total << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.250213042832911e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.001975610153749585, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00011121608258690685, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -5.364403477869928e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.1470757676288486e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0036033957730978727, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.043656643480062485, -0.026301607489585876, -0.34848445653915405, -1.7404